{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be","id":1487277,"title":"What should a vampire's innate racial abilities be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T16:58:27-07:00","id":1487277,"title":"What should a vampire's innate racial abilities be?","content":"That is, what powers should it have without any Discipline dots at all?<br /> <br /> One of the more obvious to me is that they should be able to see in the dark. I've heard various arguments for vampires not being able to see in the dark over the years, and they all fail against the sheer &quot;Dracula, Dead and Loving It&quot; silliness of a vampire stumbling around in its victim's bedroom as it fumbles for a victim it can't see.<br /> <br /> What other abilities should be innate to vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:10:46-07:00","id":1487281,"title":"","content":"I think giving Vampires Auspex 1 automatically would be a very good idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe also Potence 1 too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:21:38-07:00","id":1487284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487281#post1487281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think giving Vampires Auspex 1 automatically would be a very good idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe also Potence 1 too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celerity 1 and Fortitude 1 kind of makes sense too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:47:29-07:00","id":1487297,"title":"","content":"VtR 2e's base package seems like it captures the essentials pretty well. I don't think we need the physical Disciplines as part of the package, as blood to boost physical rolls is part of the default in VtM and VtR. VtR 2e includes enhanced senses. Lashing Out covers the classic &quot;vampire bares its fangs when suddenly confronted&quot; without needing to go full frenzy to temporarily unleash the Beast on people. <br /> <br /> A more subtle thing is that VtR 2e doesn't have Clan Weakness kick in until you drop to Humanity 6 for the first time. This hits a bunch of pop culture notes where new vampires are somewhat blank slates compared to their more experienced peers and creates the potential for in-game hope that maybe you can escape the curse of being a vampire if you fight it hard enough (you can't in the long run though). It lets you play around with fresh vampires that take time to become &quot;full&quot;vampires for both the power and price it come with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T19:13:11-07:00","id":1487302,"title":"","content":"In my games I give vampires the ability to function in general darkness without penalty. There needs to be at least some light source (starlight or the moon peeking in through the curtains or a bit of light seeping under a doorway). If a vampire were a mile under ground in absolute pitch black darkness, they'd be in as much trouble as anyone else, but functionally their night vision is naturally comparable to a cat's. Then Protean 1 can give the vampire magic glowing eyes that will let them see in the deepest darkness, or echolocation like a bat at the player's choice. Another general advantage I grant all vampires is a -1 difficulty on all rolls that involve smelling blood, or when trying to track or pinpoint someone by listening for the blood pounding in their veins.<br /> <br /> This generally means that vampires operate at better than human levels in the darkness, especially when it comes to finding and tracking prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T00:38:08-07:00","id":1487320,"title":"","content":"Nope. Vampires don't get to see in the dark automatically. Unless the moon is gone, Nights aren't that dark. There's no pressing need to really force such a power on vampires. <br /> <br /> The Awareness Talent encourages different types of supernaturals to avoid eachother. <br /> <br /> <br /> Ghoul racial abilities (often overlooked) <br /> Ghouls can increase attributes that cannot normally be improved (like Mentals) This is largely from Sires bestowing a fraction of their gains when providing ghouls blood.<br /> That +1 strength comes from the same animating force that allows vampires to move around despite not having working organs. This animating force has a lot of extra features: <br /> Ghouls don't bleed out like humans do. Some blood will escape from wounds, but it's significantly less than there should be. Being able to resist lethal damage also enables them to move on injuries that would normally keep a mortal still. <br /> Ghouls get tired a lot less, and they operate a lot better than normal people when they're tired. Operating at the bare minimum is rather like sleeping for them, and they can perform long-distance athletics with a strength of 1 indefinitely.<br /> Their ability to hold their breath or go without eating is greatly improved, especially when they're not doing much, but it isn't infinite like vampires. <br /> Of course, they can use Vitae. Vitae can be used in place of any other magic resource: Gnosis, Rage, Quintessence, Glamour, faith ETC. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires<br /> -Vampires increase attributes by feeding from many, many people with good features over their long lifespan. IE who they hunt matters. They increase Disciplines by how they hunt. <br /> -Unless they're really exerting themselves and tearing muscles (which they are more resistant to), they basically have infinite stamina when it comes to long distance athletics. <br /> -Blood bond is great. Could use better explanations of how it works. <br /> -Creating ghouls is fun and I wouldn't want that to change, but as said before, I think a Vampire's blood should work well to improve the ghoul in the long term. Much like a capitalist, the Vampire takes wealth from the masses and hands it off to his buddies. <br /> -The Vampire's internals make for a great storage space. However, most vampires can't tollerate consuming anything but blood orally. It's best to cut yourself open or use the butt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T04:49:14-07:00","id":1487362,"title":"","content":"I don't see the need to give them physical Disciplines. It also takes away somewhat from the Clans that have them as their Clan Disciplines.<ul><li>For vision, I've played it mostly like vampires can perceive part of the infrared spectrum. This enhances vision in 'normal' dark scenarios enough, while they would still be blind in a cave or something. It also gives them a sense of body heat, which is useful to pick out other undead things without Auspex.</li> <li>Sense blood sources in proximity. No exact location, but presence. Vampires being able to smell out nearby prey is a trope I like.</li> <li>Increased pain threshold, immunity to heat and cold (to the point it starts to do damage), at the price of decreased haptic senses. Dead bodies.</li> </ul><br /> I actually forgot whether or not those are already part of the default package. The rest (lick wounds to close, mini-amnesia with the bite, etc) is fine as it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T11:09:57-07:00","id":1487406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487320#post1487320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Vampires don't get to see in the dark automatically. Unless the moon is gone, Nights aren't that dark. There's no pressing need to really force such a power on vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cajun necroed the past thread on this, so you can go read that instead of me reiterating why this is not the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T12:53:48-07:00","id":1487414,"title":"","content":"I give all vampires the ability to see in the dark. I rework Protean a bit and I add a spider climbing ability.<br /> <br /> I also give all vampires enhanced physical prowess, basically just extra dice to physical attributes. One house that I sometimes use are generation dice - basically the stronger your generation the more bonus dice you get to physical attributes. Physical Disciplines are on top of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T13:57:19-07:00","id":1487416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487406#post1487406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cajun necroed the past thread on this, so you can go read that instead of me reiterating why this is not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. Gone through it.<br /> I think it's something all vampires can still work around.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malks, Toreador, Gangrel, Tremere, Tzmisce... all have their in-clan hightened senses out of the gate. So not an issue for them.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are highly social predators with ample resources and thus very likely feed in illuminated areas.<br /> Brujah, Giovanni and Lasombra either go like the Ventrue and feed through manipulation or they act like Brutes and just hit the guy till he crumples, then feed; Not a problem.<br /> Followers of Set can follow the Ventrue way of doing things until they get their own sensory power.<br /> <br /> The ones we should actually discuss.<br /> Ravnos: There's not really a need for them to fumble around in the dark. They would benefit from heightened senses helping them Sandman, because that's a safe way to feed, but the clan for the most part is transient and naturally inclined towards risky behaviour: beating mortals down for blood, manipulating them, using animals when you get desperate; this doesn't need heightened senses.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu<br /> The big one. How can they live underground without some sensory power?<br /> Well, for one, I don't think they actually put themselves that far down there, at least when we talk Neonates. Neonate Nos likely either live like other vampires, in secure homes or apartments, or they live only slightly in the underground network. In modern times, you're not hunting underground, you're just sleeping there. Either you live near enough to the entrance/exit that simple by-memory navigation is fine, or you can delve with a torch.<br /> Nosferatu are the prefect ambush predators. Feeding from the sleeping while in the dark is great for them, but they can easily gravitate towards alternatives like animal use or violence while they lack Auspex/Protean 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T14:03:14-07:00","id":1487418,"title":"","content":"This is, of course, completely skipping that vampire supposedly existed for thousands of years, and had to hunt before electricity.<br /> <br /> Also, please cite me anything that says that just because Auspex is in-Clan, means you automatically start with a dot in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T14:17:21-07:00","id":1487419,"title":"","content":"I can't put into words how much I hate the fact that vampires can't see in the dark, I'm not kidding when I say that one of the reason I switched to requiem was that they finally had fucking night vision as a natural ability, I never cared for this bullshit about vampirism being a curse, they are night predators so they should fucking see in the dark dammit, regarding masquerade I think that it didn't steal enough from requiem and what it did, it warped it too much and turned it into shit. predatory aura, enhanced senses and lashing out should have been part of the standard package from the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T14:42:37-07:00","id":1487420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487416#post1487416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. Gone through it.<br /> I think it's something all vampires can still work around.<br /> <br /> <br /> Malks, Toreador, Gangrel, Tremere, Tzmisce... all have their in-clan hightened senses out of the gate. So not an issue for them.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue are highly social predators with ample resources and thus very likely feed in illuminated areas.<br /> Brujah, Giovanni and Lasombra either go like the Ventrue and feed through manipulation or they act like Brutes and just hit the guy till he crumples, then feed; Not a problem.<br /> Followers of Set can follow the Ventrue way of doing things until they get their own sensory power.<br /> <br /> The ones we should actually discuss.<br /> Ravnos: There's not really a need for them to fumble around in the dark. They would benefit from heightened senses helping them Sandman, because that's a safe way to feed, but the clan for the most part is transient and naturally inclined towards risky behaviour: beating mortals down for blood, manipulating them, using animals when you get desperate; this doesn't need heightened senses.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu<br /> The big one. How can they live underground without some sensory power?<br /> Well, for one, I don't think they actually put themselves that far down there, at least when we talk Neonates. Neonate Nos likely either live like other vampires, in secure homes or apartments, or they live only slightly in the underground network. In modern times, you're not hunting underground, you're just sleeping there. Either you live near enough to the entrance/exit that simple by-memory navigation is fine, or you can delve with a torch.<br /> Nosferatu are the prefect ambush predators. Feeding from the sleeping while in the dark is great for them, but they can easily gravitate towards alternatives like animal use or violence while they lack Auspex/Protean 1.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I fail to see how being part of a clan should pigeonhole players into specific playstyles, all of the clans can be played in infinite ways (you would be surprised how good of an infilitrator a stealthy Ventrue could be), your idea that vampires should operate and feed only following specific patterns is faulty and would only limit the players experience just like V5 and predator types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T17:52:49-07:00","id":1487429,"title":"","content":"Vampires get all sorts of insane innate powers that facilitate being a predator - the blood bond, retractable fangs, the Kiss to paralyze victims with pleasure, the ability to regenerate from nearly any injury. It seems bizarre that they can do all of that stuff but they have to blunder around in the dark for thousands of years when the only light sources around are anathema to them - fire and the sun. They have those amazing powers but they can\u2019t even see in the dark as well as my cat can? It\u2019s just silly. It\u2019s Vampire: Dead and Loving It.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T18:16:59-07:00","id":1487432,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons I really like what VtR 2e did with Kindred senses is that they're so focused on finding blood. The default package isn't about being a cat, but about being a mosquito: homing in on food.<br /> <br /> There's a thematic strength to it, and the default package creates room for good drama (as oppose to fumbling in the dark). Hunters can learn exercises to slow their heartbeat, develop sprays to disguise the lingered scent of their living blood, and get fresh blood to fill the vampire's senses and set a trap. The hunters can become the hunted with skill, the right tools, and some luck. Sensory Disciplines are then more important for stepping beyond being a bloodsucker and into things like avoiding ambushes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T19:43:16-07:00","id":1487437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487419#post1487419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't put into words how much I hate the fact that vampires can't see in the dark, I'm not kidding when I say that one of the reason I switched to requiem was that they finally had fucking night vision as a natural ability, I never cared for this bullshit about vampirism being a curse, they are night predators so they should fucking see in the dark dammit, regarding masquerade I think that it didn't steal enough from requiem and what it did, it warped it too much and turned it into shit. predatory aura, enhanced senses and lashing out should have been part of the standard package from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pure poetry, I couldn't say it better.<br /> <br /> We can have a long discussion about other innate powers they should have. I particularly love the Requiem 2nd package for all the reasons you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> posted (the abilities to track blood are <b>really</b> fun), but if someone doesn't think it's cool, ok, I'm fine.<br /> <br /> Night vision is simply the basic. I'm not saying they must have any particular rule on night vision, just that they need to have something, or something else to complement their senses. Heck, they're nocturnal predators, they need to be able to function at night due to something other than their prey having invented the lamp.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, if I would add something to the VtR package, that would be a bonus on stealth and some forms of movement. Being a dead body that doesn't need to move at all is a superb way to not make any noise or call attention to yourself, you're basically an object. And vampires climbing, walking underwater and other such stuff are very cool ideas that, while perfectly possible within the descriptions we have, could use a small mechanical benefit to help deliver the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T23:09:47-07:00","id":1487453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487420#post1487420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I fail to see how being part of a clan should pigeonhole players into specific playstyles, all of the clans can be played in infinite ways (you would be surprised how good of an infilitrator a stealthy Ventrue could be), your idea that vampires should operate and feed only following specific patterns is faulty and would only limit the players experience just like V5 and predator types.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking at this too much from a player perspective, and in a way you're right, but in other ways you're really off the mark. <br /> <br /> 1-&quot;All of the clans can be played in infinite ways&quot; is a great idea but you can really do this more with attributes and skills and if you must, secondary disciplines. You don't need to force heightened senses on everybody to have a sneaky Ventrue that slinks around in the dark, you just need to give him a great amount of larceny and stealth and he can not-to-ambitiously work on getting a level one out-of-clan discipline if you're not satisfied. <br /> <br /> 2- Sires more often than not choose people who are like them and will thus adapt to the clan character and disciplines readily. Siring a Ventrue with poor social skills is a great way to embarass yourself and the clan. The talents of the vampire make it easier to feed a certain way, these disciplines make it easier to feed a certain way, and depending on who's game you're in either practicing these talents to feed or these Disciplines to feed will reinforce your way of hunting and the Discipline development for this style. Following this formula isn't mandatory, as you can see with point 1, but it is highly encouraged both mechanically and story-wise. If you want to play a deviant, you're setting yourself up for a challenge: Why take the easy route out and give everyone nightvision? <br /> <br /> <br /> A level one Discipline really isn't that much of an investment, and everybody should be investing a few levels into either Auspex or Protean for their other effects anyway. There's no need to give the power right from the embrace. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T01:09:14-07:00","id":1487459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487453#post1487453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're looking at this too much from a player perspective, and in a way you're right, but in other ways you're really off the mark.<br /> <br /> 1-&quot;All of the clans can be played in infinite ways&quot; is a great idea but you can really do this more with attributes and skills and if you must, secondary disciplines. You don't need to force heightened senses on everybody to have a sneaky Ventrue that slinks around in the dark, you just need to give him a great amount of larceny and stealth and he can not-to-ambitiously work on getting a level one out-of-clan discipline if you're not satisfied.<br /> <br /> 2- Sires more often than not choose people who are like them and will thus adapt to the clan character and disciplines readily. Siring a Ventrue with poor social skills is a great way to embarass yourself and the clan. The talents of the vampire make it easier to feed a certain way, these disciplines make it easier to feed a certain way, and depending on who's game you're in either practicing these talents to feed or these Disciplines to feed will reinforce your way of hunting and the Discipline development for this style. Following this formula isn't mandatory, as you can see with point 1, but it is highly encouraged both mechanically and story-wise. If you want to play a deviant, you're setting yourself up for a challenge: Why take the easy route out and give everyone nightvision?<br /> <br /> <br /> A level one Discipline really isn't that much of an investment, and everybody should be investing a few levels into either Auspex or Protean for their other effects anyway. There's no need to give the power right from the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that V5 would have turned much better if things had been approached more from a player perspective instead of trying to follow some non existent logic just because &quot;It was this way since 1st ed&quot;, giving night vision and enhanced senses (which btw, were always in as far as revised, just not mechanically so since it was only fluff) wouldn't take anything out of the game, like relly I never understood why people are so against this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T01:25:41-07:00","id":1487460,"title":"","content":"There's also a reason I keep pointing to VtR 2e here. Kindred Senses in VtR 2e makes Auspex 1-3 and Protean 2 <b>so much</b> better because they don't need to waste time on some boosted senses. VtR 2e's lower levels of Auspex allow way more creativity on both sides of the ST screen because it's not just a boost to Perception, and Protean 2 lets you manifest fully functional non-human sensory organs. By making better senses a mechanical reality of the base vampire package, you're also letting the Disciplines that enhance senses to do way cooler shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T02:00:17-07:00","id":1487462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487459#post1487459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that V5 would have turned much better if things had been approached more from a player perspective instead of trying to follow some non existent logic just because &quot;It was this way since 1st ed&quot;, giving night vision and enhanced senses (which btw, were always in as far as revised, just not mechanically so since it was only fluff) wouldn't take anything out of the game, like relly I never understood why people are so against this.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>-Non existent logic-</i><br /> Alright, this is the attitude of an unreasonable person. There's certainly logic behind it. Vampires don't fucking <i>need</i> night vision. It's as simple as that. It's useful. It's not essential. &quot;Vampires need night vision to function because they function at night hur hur hur&quot; is such empty headed drivel. No. They don't need better than human vision at night, players just need to get good at the game and play according to their character. Your character shouldn't start with the best abilities from Auspex, Dominate, Celerity, Potence, Presence, Protean and Thaumaturgy just because you personally are dead set on matching some bullshit dracula concept you've got in your head. This is why the lore states most fledglings don't make it: because being a vampire is <i>hard.</i> You are weak, you are vulnerable, you make mistakes, you'll die if you're not smart about it. Rise to the occasion; don't expect the occasion to fall to your level.<br /> <br /> &quot;from a player perspective&quot; is a good way to cut all the art out of the game and get a soulless corperate product. People don't play story heavy games like VTM to have an easy time, they play to have an <i>interesting</i> time. VTM's central theme is the Jyhadd, the eternal struggle. The setting is also satire, a spirited attack on the ruling class and the ills of the world; if your transhuman elite is fumbling in the dark, that's not a bad thing. Part of the joys of VTM is laughing at your own mistakes. How fragile do you need to be to want to do everything perfectly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T04:07:49-07:00","id":1487470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487462#post1487462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>-Non existent logic-</i><br /> Alright, this is the attitude of an unreasonable person. There's certainly logic behind it. Vampires don't fucking <i>need</i> night vision. It's as simple as that. It's useful. It's not essential. &quot;Vampires need night vision to function because they function at night hur hur hur&quot; is such empty headed drivel. No. They don't need better than human vision at night, players just need to get good at the game and play according to their character. Your character shouldn't start with the best abilities from Auspex, Dominate, Celerity, Potence, Presence, Protean and Thaumaturgy just because you personally are dead set on matching some bullshit dracula concept you've got in your head. This is why the lore states most fledglings don't make it: because being a vampire is <i>hard.</i> You are weak, you are vulnerable, you make mistakes, you'll die if you're not smart about it. Rise to the occasion; don't expect the occasion to fall to your level.<br /> <br /> &quot;from a player perspective&quot; is a good way to cut all the art out of the game and get a soulless corperate product. People don't play story heavy games like VTM to have an easy time, they play to have an <i>interesting</i> time. VTM's central theme is the Jyhadd, the eternal struggle. The setting is also satire, a spirited attack on the ruling class and the ills of the world; if your transhuman elite is fumbling in the dark, that's not a bad thing. Part of the joys of VTM is laughing at your own mistakes. How fragile do you need to be to want to do everything perfectly?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Speaking of bullshit concepts in one's own head, I fail to see where in the fuck is written that vampires don't need night vision, you seem to be the one fixated on a very personal interpretation of what vampires in masquerade are, the book is very clear in the starting fluff that kindred acquire enhanced senses at the embrace, they just never gave mechanics for it, Auspex doesn't give you night vision it just lowers the difficulty of perception rolls, protean is the only one that gives you night vision and it is supposed to see through even magically enhanced darkness, vampires having nightvision on par of what you would expect from a nocturnal predator is effectively supported by the fluff, they just never bothered to come up with anything for it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">About vampire life being hard that is definitely true but If you think that giving them night vision will make it a breeze then you really should read the books again, neonates life is shit because they die and wake up in a feudal society whose rulers couldn't give less of a shit about them and are ready to sacrifice them in whatever petty scheme they concocted that week, the vampiric condition on itself, while definitely no cakewalk, is far from being the main factor, as far as them being weak, that is only true by comparison to other vampires and supernaturals (and even that is debatable, you damn well know you can make an elder killing machine with celerity, obtenebration and resilience straight out of character creation), compared to humans, even the weakest, newest neonate is still superior to them, the book never even tried to hide vampire's individual superiority compared to humans.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regarding the &quot;artistic qualities&quot; of WoD, well, my introduction to it was with masquerade revised so I'm not as high on the pole of grandmasters edgelords but, from what I have read since then, most of the oWoD products were crocks of shit that looked like they were written by a 12 years old in his goth phase, the framework of WoD is extremely creative and very unique but let's not pretend that most of the books were any more artistic than an indie comic book, the quality improved from the late 2000's onward (untill taking a dive again with V5 unfortunately). The setting being a satire is irrelevant to the power fantasy of playing as a vampire because yes, people play masquerade also to have cool vampire powers and do cool shit, the doom and gloom comes later when the sects starts taking an interest and make your (most likely short) unlife an unliving hell, failure is part of any rpg system and it can be fun but I can't see how such a minor mechanic would lessen it, how fragile do you need to be to fear change that much?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 07-22-2022, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T04:46:36-07:00","id":1487473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487470#post1487470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I fail to see where in the fuck is written that vampires don't need night vision</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's the default state, so they don't really need to write such a thing do they? The implication is there. Did you see it written that they need night vision somewhere? I sure haven't, and most characters I've played with have gotten along fine without it. And yeah, I'm a stickler for things like this, I'd notice if a lack of night vision would be a problem in a scenario. It's an easily avoidable problem. <br /> <br /> (Heightened senses doubles the clarity and range of senses. That's enough to get by regular darkness. Pitch darkness is rare, and a vampire with Heightened senses can still navigate with sound/smell/touch etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T05:20:53-07:00","id":1487476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487473#post1487473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it's the default state, so they don't really need to write such a thing do they? The implication is there. Did you see it written that they need night vision somewhere? I sure haven't, and most characters I've played with have gotten along fine without it. And yeah, I'm a stickler for things like this, I'd notice if a lack of night vision would be a problem in a scenario. It's an easily avoidable problem.<br /> <br /> (Heightened senses doubles the clarity and range of senses. That's enough to get by regular darkness. Pitch darkness is rare, and a vampire with Heightened senses can still navigate with sound/smell/touch etc)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it isn't written anywhere that they don't have night vision, the rest is only your idea of why a vampire shouldn't need night vision, what is written is that &quot;Upon the Embrace, the fledgling\u2019s senses sharpen, displaying to her a richness of visual colors, auditory distinction, tactile fineness, and olfactory alertness that mortals senses are too limited to discern.&quot; that seems a clear indication that vampire do indeed see better in the dark than your average human but the writers never added any mechanics for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T07:21:05-07:00","id":1487478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487476#post1487476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So it isn't written anywhere that they don't have night vision, the rest is only your idea of why a vampire shouldn't need night vision</div> </div> </div> </div>They can acquire nightvision. <br /> Protean 1. <br /> Auspex 1 works pretty well too. <br /> <br /> <br /> There are clearly specific powers that do the thing you think should be default. IE nightvision isn't available by default. <br /> They have to spend XP for it, or acquire it at character gen.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what is written is that &quot;Upon the Embrace, the fledgling\u2019s senses sharpen, displaying to her a richness of visual colors, auditory distinction, tactile fineness, and olfactory alertness that mortals senses are too limited to discern.&quot; that seems a clear indication that vampire do indeed see better in the dark than your average human but the writers never added any mechanics for it. </div> </div> </div>Sure, this is written, but it's vague. A hypothetical 5 or 10 percent increase in colour saturation is very noticeable but it isn't enough to provide a mechanical benefit or an ability to see in the dark. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T07:59:57-07:00","id":1487480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487277-what-should-a-vampire-s-innate-racial-abilities-be?p=1487478#post1487478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can acquire nightvision.<br /> Protean 1.<br /> Auspex 1 works pretty well too.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are clearly specific powers that do the thing you think should be default. IE nightvision isn't available by default.<br /> They have to spend XP for it, or acquire it at character gen.<br /> <br /> Sure, this is written, but it's vague. A hypothetical 5 or 10 percent increase in colour saturation is very noticeable but it isn't enough to provide a mechanical benefit or an ability to see in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Auspex doesn't give you night vision, the book even specifies that it just lowers the difficulty brought by the penalty (same effect but still not the same), Protean gives you perfect night vision in complete darkness and even supernatural one if I remember correctly, it is not the same as the kind of night vision an animal would have, requiem thought about this by giving a penalty for complete darkness while &quot;normal&quot; darkness, the kind humans wouldn't be able to see in, would give no such penalty.<br /> <br /> Regarding the text being vague, who says that is the only increase? They might actually have the kind of night vision a cat would have, plenty of art despict vampires with a glow in their eyes similar to the tapetum lucidum many animals have to see better in the dark, besides, as vague as the text is, it is still more than your opinions on why vampires don't need night vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}